    {
      "id": "e218",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1130,
      "y": 748,
      "width": 698.8170126086897,
      "height": 30,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1786319717504,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. Sleeve, not a cored hole with cables threaded through it. The sleeve is what lets the next\nperson add a cable without breaking the fire rating and the clean-agent hold time.",
      "originalText": "1. Sleeve, not a cored hole with cables threaded through it. The sleeve is what lets the next person add a cable without breaking the fire rating and the clean-agent hold time.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "version": 12,
      "versionNonce": 576384827,
      "index": "b2V",
      "isDeleted": false,
      "seed": 1,
      "autoResize": false
    },
    {
      "id": "e219",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1130,
      "y": 795,
      "width": 694.4085789548666,
      "height": 30,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1786319740573,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "2. Install spare sleeves on any wall you cannot cheaply reopen. Cap both sides with the same\nfirestop assembly and leave a mule tape inside.",
      "originalText": "2. Install spare sleeves on any wall you cannot cheaply reopen. Cap both sides with the same firestop assembly and leave a mule tape inside.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "version": 19,
      "versionNonce": 989091989,
      "index": "b2W",
      "isDeleted": false,
      "seed": 1,
      "autoResize": false
    },
    {
      "id": "e220",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1130,
      "y": 839,
      "width": 690,
      "height": 30,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1786319785044,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "3. Bond every metallic sleeve at one end - typically the server-room end - to the TGB with #6 AWG,\nhome run. See E-302.",
      "originalText": "3. Bond every metallic sleeve at one end - typically the server-room end - to the TGB with #6 AWG, home run. See E-302.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "version": 36,
      "versionNonce": 1592934197,
      "index": "b2X",
      "isDeleted": false,
      "seed": 1,
      "autoResize": false
